-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- SCENARIO A — CTL violation (C1: Power Gate)
-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Purpose: Show NuSMV producing a finite-path counterexample for a violated AG property.
--
-- Step 1: Copy mars_rover_fixed.smv to mars_rover_faulty_A.smv
-- Step 2: In NavModule's next(nav_state), replace the IDLE block's power check:
--
--   ORIGINAL (correct):
--     nav_state = IDLE & power_state = CRITICAL : IDLE;
--     nav_state = IDLE & power_fault_active      : IDLE;
--
--   FAULTY (remove both power guards):
--     nav_state = IDLE : DRIVING;   -- BUG: power check removed
--
-- Step 3: Run: nusmv mars_rover_faulty_A.smv
--
-- Expected NuSMV output:
--   -- specification AG (power.power_state = CRITICAL ->
--        nav.nav_state != DRIVING & nav.nav_state != AUTONAV)  is false
--   -- as demonstrated by the following execution sequence
--   Trace Description: CTL Counterexample
--   Trace Type: Counterexample
--   -> State: 1.1 <-     nav_state=IDLE,  power_state=NOMINAL
--   -> State: 1.2 <-     nav_state=DRIVING, power_state=NOMINAL
--   -> State: 1.3 <-     nav_state=DRIVING, power_state=LOW
--   -> State: 1.4 <-     nav_state=DRIVING, power_state=CRITICAL   <-- VIOLATION
--
-- Counterexample structure: FINITE PATH (no loop) — CTL always gives shortest
-- path to a state where the invariant fails.

-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- SCENARIO B — LTL violation (L1: Safe Mode Until)
-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Purpose: Show NuSMV producing a lasso-shaped counterexample for a violated
--          LTL Until property.
--
-- Step 1: Copy mars_rover_fixed.smv to mars_rover_faulty_B.smv
-- Step 2: In NavModule's next(nav_state), replace the OBSTACLE_DETECTED transition:
--
--   ORIGINAL (correct):
--     nav_state = OBSTACLE_DETECTED & comm_state = BLACKOUT & power_state = LOW : SAFE_MODE;
--     nav_state = OBSTACLE_DETECTED & power_state = CRITICAL                    : SAFE_MODE;
--     nav_state = OBSTACLE_DETECTED & comm_state = AUTOMODE                     : SAFE_MODE;
--     nav_state = OBSTACLE_DETECTED                                              : REPLANNING;
--
--   FAULTY (bypass SAFE_MODE entirely):
--     nav_state = OBSTACLE_DETECTED : DRIVING;   -- BUG: skips SAFE_MODE
--
-- Step 3: Run: nusmv mars_rover_faulty_B.smv
--
-- Expected NuSMV output:
--   -- specification G (power.power_fault_active ->
--        (nav.nav_state != DRIVING) U (nav.nav_state = SAFE_MODE))  is false
--   -- as demonstrated by the following execution sequence
--   Trace Description: LTL Counterexample
--   Trace Type: Counterexample
--   -> State: 1.1 <-   nav_state=IDLE,              power_fault_active=FALSE
--   -> State: 1.2 <-   nav_state=DRIVING,            power_fault_active=FALSE
--   -> State: 1.3 <-   nav_state=OBSTACLE_DETECTED,  power_fault_active=TRUE
--   -- Loop starts here --
--   -> State: 1.4 <-   nav_state=DRIVING,            power_fault_active=TRUE  <-- VIOLATION
--
-- Counterexample structure: LASSO (prefix + infinite loop) — LTL always gives
-- a lasso because LTL properties are about infinite executions.
-- The "-- Loop starts here --" annotation marks the start of the repeating suffix.
-- The Until condition is never satisfied on this looping path.

-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Key structural difference between CTL and LTL counterexamples:
-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- CTL (Scenario A): Finite path ending at the violating state.
--   NuSMV finds the shortest path to a state where AG's argument fails.
--   No loop annotation in the output.
--
-- LTL (Scenario B): Lasso = finite prefix + loop.
--   NuSMV must exhibit an infinite path because LTL properties quantify
--   over infinite executions. The loop shows the Until condition is never met.
--   Output includes "-- Loop starts here --" before the looping state.
-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
